## Migration Plan

How do we transition from current to proposed canon without breaking consumers?

### Phase 1 — Communication
- [ ] Affected parties notified
- [ ] Migration timeline communicated

### Phase 2 — Parallel state (optional, if backward compatibility required)
- [ ] New canon active alongside old canon
- [ ] Clear deprecation signal on old canon

### Phase 3 — Cutover
- [ ] Old canon removed
- [ ] New canon in sole effect
- [ ] Documentation updated
- [ ] Tests updated

### Phase 4 — Verification
- [ ] Architecture lint passed
- [ ] Contract lint passed
- [ ] Local CI passed
- [ ] Relevant pytest suite passed
- [ ] Documentation links updated
- [ ] No competing canon remains undocumented

## Backward Compatibility

Can existing consumers adopt the change without breaking?

- [ ] Fully backward compatible — no action required from consumers
- [ ] Grace period required — migration plan above
- [ ] Breaking change — consumer migration required, timeline documented

